    {
      "id": 140065,
      "name": "bluedarky",
      "username": "bluedarky",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-01T14:07:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Chrono\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chrono/48/2334_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Chrono:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I thought Baron Blade ran the medical testing that gave Setback his powers. Does he own or work for this evil corporation?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Personally, I think that they just follow the money. &nbsp;We know Baron Blade is definately involved in RevoCorp though as RevoCorp tech is seen on Rebuilt to Survive in Fright Train's deck (and Blade provides the card quote) and the Villains blog for Plague Rat mentions that RevoCorp sent him out to hunt down Setback after he escaped from their lab.</p>",
